1: {"body":"## The gap

The engine-side profile answers "how long did `g3d` take", but not "which part of the game asked for it". On sinjoh I spent a day guessing at where the field's 4.3 ms of logic went; two rounds of wrong guesses later, a cheap game-side probe put 2.1 ms of it in one function (`ApplicationManager_Exec` of the field map app) and 236 us in another, in a single run. Without that, every optimization is a guess about which of twenty calls to attack.

This is the facility. It is ~30 lines in the engine and ~10 in the profile print, and it is what produced the attribution table in sinjoh's STATUS (`docs/STATUS.md`, sixth pass).

## Engine side (`src/runtime/kj_bridge.h`, `src/runtime/kj_frame.c`, `src/graphics/renderer.c`)

```c
/* kj_bridge.h */
#define KJ_PROBE_SLOTS 11
/* in kj_ds_profile: */
uint64_t probe_ticks[KJ_PROBE_SLOTS];
uint64_t probe_calls[KJ_PROBE_SLOTS];
```

```c
/* kj_frame.c */
static u64 s_probe_ticks[KJ_PROBE_SLOTS];
static u32 s_probe_calls[KJ_PROBE_SLOTS];

u64 NitroPort_ProbeNow(void) { return svcGetSystemTick(); }

void NitroPort_NoteProbeSince(unsigned slot, u64 t0)
{
    if (slot < KJ_PROBE_SLOTS) {
        s_probe_ticks[slot] += svcGetSystemTick() - t0;
        ++s_probe_calls[slot];
    }
}
/* take_profile: copy + zero both arrays so each window reports its own total */
```

```c
/* renderer.c, the [ds] window line */
kj_log("[probe] per game frame: slot 0 %llu us, 1 %llu us, ...", ...);
```

## Game side (temporary, removed after measuring)

```c
const u64 probeAll = NitroPort_ProbeNow();
u64 probeT = probeAll;
HandleFieldInput(fieldSystem);
NitroPort_NoteProbeSince(1, probeT); probeT = NitroPort_ProbeNow();
...
NitroPort_NoteProbeSince(0, probeAll);
```

## Three things that cost me time, so they are worth encoding

1. **Use `svcGetSystemTick`, never `OS_GetTick`.** `OS_GetTick` goes through the port's timer emulation, which syncs DS timers: measured at ~8 us per frame... (line truncated to 2000 chars)
