```
→
```c
const kj_tile_ref t = kj_atlas_tile(source, c->bg_vram + toff, toff, bpp8, pal, pal_id);
run_note(out, t.slot, toff, tile_bytes);
if (!t.valid || t.transparent) {
    continue;
}
```
Wait — for !t.valid (atlas full, slot never assigned): t.slot = 0 and ref invalid. run_note records range ✓, and continue ✓.

But careful: in the retained reuse check, kj_atlas_touch(slots, count) — slots beyond count untouched ✓.

objs():
```c
const kj_tile_ref t = kj_atlas_tile(source, c->obj_vram + off, off, bpp8, pal, pal_id);
if (!t.valid || t.transparent) continue;
run_note(out, t.slot, off, tile_bytes);
```
same fix.

Also update the comment at 824-832 ("the exact range of character bytes the build read") to note that blank tiles are tracked too. Add a sentence.

Then rebuild kj-prof (~15 min) and re-run the freeze capture drive. Also commit as issue #1 fix along with pokegear.py + layer_split.py + freeze_cap.py tools.

Wait — one more check before rebuilding: does this ACTUALLY explain the symptom? At the call-open rebuild, body tiles blank → range recorded including body toffs (0xAEA0..0xAF60). Later glyph writes → memcmp fails → rebuild → text renders. YES.

But hold on — why was there only ONE rebuild in the 600-frame window (t=301 cycle covers 9050-9650) and NONE in the following window? With the bug, glyph writes happen but no rebuild → reused 6000, rebuilt 0 ✓ consistent.

Also — the label rendering: label glyphs were present at the call-open rebuild → built ✓.

Edge: the pokegear clock digits ("00:05" minutes) — same hole? The clock digits change every minute — those are likely map-entry changes (SBB content changes) → map compare catches it ✓.

One more consideration: this bug affects ANY layer where glyph data is written into previously-blank tiles without a map change — the opening-movie starter particles? Those are 3D/OBJ. Anyway.

Apply the fix now.

