Now write the host.json via launch.ps1 -ConfigureOnly with fixture, plus asset_directories for build outputs. But launch.ps1's param doesn't support asset_directories; it writes host.json without it. Better: craft host.json myself (launch.ps1 -ConfigureOnly writes worker/storage_root/assets/allow_control). I'll write host.json manually with asset_directories, then add the opencode MCP config using launch.ps1 -Mode WindowedMCP -Fixture <kj-prof 3dsx>.

host.json fields: worker = runtimes/citnlo/ctr-worker.exe, storage_root = data/citnlo/sessions, assets: {homebrew?} — assets map in host config: {"demo": path}? In v0.0.3 assets used handles like 'kohjoh-prof/pokeheartgold.3dsx' — handle 'kohjoh-prof' with asset_directories... but asset_directories is new in v0.0.4. Use asset_directories: {"kohjoh-prof": "C:/Users/terezi/workdir/kohjoh/build/kj-prof"}? That maps handle → dir, each .3dsx inside approved as <handle>/<file>: so asset "kohjoh-prof/pokeheartgold.3dsx" — matches the old naming! Great.

Also maybe add sinjoh dir and hotpath builds. Add handles: "kohjoh-prof" → kj-prof, "kohjoh" → build/kj? and sinjoh card's own 3dsx are on its sdmc (loaded via card?). Keep simple: asset_directories for kj-prof + hotpath-prof + sinjoh build dir if exists.

Then opencode.json mcp config:

"mcp": {
  "lotus": {
    "type": "local",
    "command": ["powershell.exe", "-NoProfile", "-ExecutionPolicy", "Bypass", "-File", "C:\\Users\\terezi\\workdir\\LOTUS-v0.0.4-windows-x64\\launch.ps1", "-Mode", "WindowedMCP"],
    "enabled": true,
    "environment": {}
  }
}

Check opencode MCP config format — v0.x: {"mcp": {"<name>": {"type": "local", "command": [...], "enabled": true, "environment": {...}}}}. Yes.

Also the bridge python (sinjoh/tools/lotus/bridge.py port 45761) — the old workflow. MCP replaces it. But our existing drivers (ctl.py etc.) talk to the bridge; keep bridge option but MCP is requested. Also check sinjoh tools for an MCP client wrapper? Not needed.

Write host.json via launch.ps1 -ConfigureOnly -Fixture kj-prof 3dsx, then append asset_directories by editing host.json (launch.ps1 rewrites host.json each run — note: it overwrites! So asset_directories added manually would be lost whenever launch.ps1 runs again. Hmm. But launch.ps1 -Mode WindowedMCP rewrites host.json each time, wiping asset_directories. Since opencode launches via launch.ps1, that's a problem.

Alternative: don't use launch.ps1 in opencode config; invoke bin/lotus-desktop.exe --mcp host.json directly with a hand-written host.json. That keeps asset_directories. Windowed mode = lotus-desktop --mcp (the window shows too). That satisfies "MCP launches in windowed mode".

